| 001-435 targeted waits and pending discovery ([GitHub #17](https://github.com/hearsay-tools/squeal/issues/17), agent friction) | planned (triaged 2026-10-16; HOLD for the human, no implementation dispatched) | Evidence and replay: `specifications/001-core-loop/research/issue-17.md`, `research/probes/issue-17/README.md`. On shipped 0.1.199, a named unit wait selected 3 broad-input slow dependents and exited 3 at 30.2 s though the unit result arrived at 390 ms; config/touch during a fast run held discovery and new-file listing until that run ended; config re-key showed queued checks and running 0 while a run was open. A restart requirement did not reproduce: listing recovered after completion or timeout. Aligned with vision principles 2, 3, 4 and 7, and the decision filter's timely, trustworthy pull state. Related rows: 005-11 and 006-55 (named waits), 001-150/001-228 (runner work and its bound), 001-381 (edit behind backlog), 004-11/004-30/001-376 (shared slow resources). New information: test-path selection differs from 005 D2; pending discovery omits phase/reason/bound; running 0 obscures in-flight work; edit-behind-edit waiting extends 001-381's question. Surface these to the human before choosing repairs; requested target priority would revisit 005-11's human decision of 2026-10-13, not silently override it. Original cezarion stall cause remains unconfirmed; its retained rows may expire around 2026-10-23. | Human chooses next steps and scope, recorded in status.md and separate implementation rows if approved. Any approved work preserves pending/unknown provenance and has regressions for exact-file selection, bounded discovery diagnostics and new-file discovery without restart. This triage is not approval to implement. |
